    "question": {
      ":question/id": "dc7667da-11cd-588c-a5a5-aeebc93d3012",
      ":question/problem": "What is the augmented matrix for the following system of linear equations?\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-11y-6x-21z &=18 \\\\ 3x+4y &=-23z \\\\ -1+15y &=x\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First, we organize the system so that the variables are ordered $x,y,z$ on the left-hand side, the constants are on the right-hand side, and every variable has a coefficient:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-6x-11y-21z &=18 \\\\ 3x+4y+23z &=0 \\\\ -x+15y+0z &=1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe coefficient matrix consists of the coefficients of the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-6 & -11 & -21 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 23 \\\\ -1 & 15 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe augmented matrix is the coefficient matrix augmented with the column that represents the right-hand sides of the equations:\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}-6 & -11 & -21 & 18 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 23 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 15 & 0 & 1\\end{array}\\right]\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
